# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  DEVELOPMENT TEMPLATE.  Copy to `.env.local`, then fill it in.
#
#  EVERY `VITE_` VALUE IS PUBLIC.
#  Vite compiles them into the JavaScript a browser downloads. A key written
#  here is a key anyone can read by opening the bundle, and the only repair is
#  to rotate it. Secrets belong in the SERVER's environment, never here.
#
#  `src/canvas/api/envPolicy.test.ts` reads this file on every test run and
#  fails if a secret-shaped `VITE_` name is given a value -- commented out or
#  not, because uncommenting is one keystroke.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# WHERE THE BACKEND IS.  Public: the address of a server is not a way into it.
# Empty means same origin, which is what you want in development. `vite.config.ts`
# proxies /api/ask, /api/lesson, /api/day, /api/done and /api/health to the
# planner on http://127.0.0.1:8787. Set this only when the API is on another host.
VITE_API_BASE=

# WEB SEARCH.  Leave the endpoint blank and the tutor honestly reports that it
# cannot look things up, rather than inventing sources.
VITE_SEARCH_ENDPOINT=
# `research` reads the pages it finds; anything else uses the engine alone.
VITE_SEARCH_DEPTH=

# --- THESE STAY EMPTY --------------------------------------------------------
# The tutor asks this project's own backend, which holds the model key
# server-side (see `server/provider.ts`). The browser never needs one.
#
# Put your real key in the SERVER's environment instead:
#     GROQ_API_KEY=...   or   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...   or   GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#
# Setting the variable below anyway is allowed for a LOCAL model runner that
# wants a placeholder, and the app warns you on the console that you have
# published it. Committing a value here fails the test suite.
VITE_TUTOR_KEY=
VITE_SEARCH_KEY=
